Unstructured HTML/EBB Table Extraction. Interstate pipeline Electronic Bulletin Boards (like Kinder Morgan or TC Energy) frequently alter HTML table layouts. Agents pass raw HTML snippets to Ollama with format: "json" enforced to extract the exact scalar value (Dth/d) without brittle regex rules breaking.
Point-in-Time Release Timestamp Extraction. Many EIA reports and pipeline critical notices bury the publication timestamp in text headers (e.g., "Posted November 11, 2026 at 10:30 AM EST"). Ollama converts these messy strings into strict UTC ISO-8601 available_timestamp values to prevent look-ahead bias in your backtest.
Pre-Database Sanity & Outlier Gatekeeping. Before writing to your database, each agent sends the newly scraped value alongside its trailing 30-day mean and standard deviation to Ollama. The model flags unit-conversion errors (such as MMBtu accidentally reported instead of Bcf) before bad data corrupts your historical time series.
Self-Healing Scraper Selector Repair. When a source URL returns a 404 or empty parse, a fallback agent sends the updated webpage DOM to your local Ollama instance to identify the new CSS selector or query parameter automatically.
