Because your agents communicate over the public internet to your local Ubuntu GPU, optimize your Cloudflare Tunnel (cloudflared) to prevent dropped connections and unauthorized access:
Prevent 403 Forbidden Host Rejections. In your Cloudflare Zero Trust Tunnel Public Hostname settings, set HTTP Host Header to localhost:11434 (or set OLLAMA_ORIGINS="*" on Ubuntu) so Ollama accepts incoming tunnel packets.
Increase Proxy Read Timeouts. Set Cloudflare's Proxy Read Timeout to 120s so batch bursts from all 81 agents do not trigger 524 Timeout errors while waiting in the GPU queue.
Lock Down with Service Tokens. Create a Cloudflare Access Service Token (CF-Access-Client-Id and CF-Access-Client-Secret) and inject those two headers into your Python agent base class so only your 81 agents can reach your local GPU.
